{"id": "d641422b-f782-404b-a264-c52e6b5725fe", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I wasn't able to verify the exact numbering from the docs, but I recall 4.1.7 in the CIS EKS benchmark (v1.4+) referring to avoiding the system:masters group, listed as Level 1, Manual, with a FAIL status—though I should flag the caveat that numbering may differ across benchmark versions.

Looking at the config, mapUsers maps alice directly to system:masters, which bypasses RBAC entirely since that group can't be restricted by normal authorization. Since authenticationMode is API_AND_CONFIG_MAP, the aws-auth ConfigMap mapping is still actively enforced (it would be ignored only in API-only mode), so this is a real violation—remediation means creating a scoped EKS access entry for alice, removing the mapUsers binding, and eventually migrating to API-only mode, while making sure she has replacement access first.

"}]}
